    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "After an acute S pyogenesinfection, there is a\nlatent period of 1–4 WEEKS (mean 7 days),\nafter which nephritis or rheumatic fever\noccasionally develops. The latent period\nsuggests that these poststreptococcal\ndiseases are not attributable to the direct\neffect of disseminated bacteria but instead\nrepresent a hypersensitivity response.\nNephritis is more commonly preceded by\ninfection of the skin; rheumatic fever is more\ncommonly preceded by infection of the\nrespiratory tract Jawetz Medical\nMicrobiology 27th ed p. 218",
