    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "People with chronic granulomatous disease\n(NADPH oxidase deficiency) have recurrent\ninfections with certain CATalase organisms.\nExamples: Nocardia, Pseudomonas, Listeria,\nAspergillus, Candida, E coli, Staphylococci,\nSerratia, B cepacia, H pylori. CATs Need\nPLACESS to Belch their Hairballs. USMLE\nStep1 First Aid 2017",
