    "id": "notion-microbiology-0007",
    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 7,
    "stem": "Which is the most common viral infection of the reproductive system?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Molluscum contagiosum"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "HIV"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Human Papilloma Virus"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Genital Herpes"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Human papillomaviruses are the most common sexually transmitted viruses and include strains that cause genital warts as well as strains that cause cervical cancer. Several strains of HPV cause venereal warts, the most common STD. Some types (most commonly 16 and 18) are also associated with cervical dysplasia and cervical intraepithelial neoplasia.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Molluscum contagiosum is a viral infection caused by the molluscum contagiosum virus. It primarily affects the skin and mucous membranes, including the genital area. While it can be sexually transmitted, it is not as common in the reproductive system as other viral infections. It typically presents as small, raised, and painless bumps on the skin.",
      "B": "HIV is a virus that primarily targets the immune system, leading to acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS). While HIV can be transmitted through sexual contact, it affects the immune system rather than causing visible lesions or symptoms in the reproductive system. It is a serious and life-threatening infection that can lead to various complications if not managed properly.",
      "C": "Human papillomaviruses are the most common sexually transmitted viruses and include strains that cause genital warts as well as strains that cause cervical cancer. Several strains of HPV cause venereal warts, the most common STD. Some types (most commonly 16 and 18) are also associated with cervical dysplasia and cervical intraepithelial neoplasia.",
      "D": "Genital herpes is caused by the herpes simplex virus (HSV) and is a common sexually transmitted infection. HSV type 2 is more commonly associated with genital herpes, while HSV type 1 can also cause genital infections. It presents with painful sores or blisters in the genital area and can recur periodically."
    },
