    "id": "notion-microbiology-0032",
    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 32,
    "stem": "Situation 6 - A female sex worker developed purulent vaginal discharge but failed to seek medical treatment. Later she developed papules and pustules on her hands, forearm, and legs. What finally prompted her to seek medical consult was when she had painful swelling of her wrists.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Gouty arthritis"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Gonococcal arthritis"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "TB synovitis"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Hemorrhagic arthritis"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "The patient presented with purulent vaginal discharge and works as a female sex worker. Disseminated gonococcal infections include septic arthritis, wherein Neisseria gonorrhoeae is the most common cause in sexually active adults. In this form of disseminated infection, there is presence of arthritis, tenosynovitis, or pustules in the skin as seen on the patient.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Gouty arthritis is caused by the deposition of monosodium urate crystals in joints, leading to inflammation. It typically presents with sudden, severe pain, redness, and swelling in the affected joint. Gout is not directly associated with purulent vaginal discharge or a history of sex work.",
      "B": "The patient presented with purulent vaginal discharge and works as a female sex worker. Disseminated gonococcal infections include septic arthritis, wherein Neisseria gonorrhoeae is the most common cause in sexually active adults. In this form of disseminated infection, there is presence of arthritis, tenosynovitis, or pustules in the skin as seen on the patient.",
      "C": "Tuberculosis (TB) synovitis is a form of extrapulmonary tuberculosis that can affect the joints. It may present with joint pain and swelling. However, the patient's occupation as a sex worker and the presence of purulent vaginal discharge make gonococcal arthritis a more likely diagnosis.",
      "D": "Hemorrhagic arthritis is not a specific diagnosis. Joint bleeding can occur in various conditions, including bleeding disorders or trauma. It is not directly associated with the patient's symptoms and occupation."
    },
