    "id": "notion-microbiology-0076",
    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 76,
    "stem": "Which of the following characteristics distinguishes this organism on differential media?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Inability to ferment lactose"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Its somatic O antigen"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Ability to ferment glucose"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Ability to ferment mannitol"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Shigella dysenteriae is a non-lactose fermenter. It does not utilize lactose, which distinguishes it on differential media. Most Shigella species, including S. dysenteriae, do not produce gas from the fermentation of glucose.\nNo H2S production\nNon-lactose fermenter\nProduce no gas from the fermentation of glucose",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Shigella dysenteriae is a non-lactose fermenter. It does not utilize lactose, which distinguishes it on differential media. Most Shigella species, including S. dysenteriae, do not produce gas from the fermentation of glucose.\nNo H2S production\nNon-lactose fermenter\nProduce no gas from the fermentation of glucose",
      "B": "The somatic O antigen is a characteristic used for the serotyping of bacteria, particularly in the Enterobacteriaceae family. While it helps differentiate various strains within the Shigella species, it may not be the most practical characteristic for routine identification on differential media.",
      "C": "Shigella dysenteriae can ferment glucose. However, the ability to ferment glucose is a common feature among Enterobacteriaceae, and it may not be a specific characteristic for differentiating Shigella dysenteriae from other members of the family.",
      "D": "Shigella dysenteriae does not typically ferment mannitol. The fermentation of mannitol is often used to differentiate between species, and the inability to ferment it can be a characteristic that distinguishes Shigella dysenteriae from some other bacteria."
    },
