    "id": "notion-microbiology-0083",
    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 83,
    "stem": "Situation 23 - A 60-year old smoker developed productive cough with associated fever and chills, and shortness of breath. Sputum gram-stain revealed neutrophils with very few organisms that stain poorly with gram stain but are positive with silver. Culture showed gray-white textured glass appearance when grown on charcoal yeast extract with iron and cysteine.",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Haemophilus influenza"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Streptococcus pneumonia"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Legionella pneumophila"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Moraxella catarrhalis"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Legionella Pneumophilia – Gram (-) rod. Gram stains poorly – use silver stain. Grown on charcoal yeast extract medium with iron and cysteine. Colonies are round or flat with entire edges. They vary in color from colorless to iridescent pink or blue and are translucent or speckled. Legionnaire’s disease – severe pneumonia, fever, GI and CNS symptoms",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Haemophilus influenza – small gram (-) coccobacillary rod. Culture on chocolate agar, which contains factors V and X. Mucosal infections (otitis media, conjunctivitis, bronchitis) as well as invasive infections. Does not cause the flu.",
      "B": "Streptococcus pneumonia is a gram-positive, alpha-hemolytic, lancet-shaped diplococcus. It is a common cause of pneumonia, especially in individuals with risk factors such as advanced age or underlying health conditions.",
      "C": "Legionella Pneumophilia – Gram (-) rod. Gram stains poorly – use silver stain. Grown on charcoal yeast extract medium with iron and cysteine. Colonies are round or flat with entire edges. They vary in color from colorless to iridescent pink or blue and are translucent or speckled. Legionnaire’s disease – severe pneumonia, fever, GI and CNS symptoms",
      "D": "Moraxella catarrhalis is a gram-negative diplococcus. It can cause respiratory tract infections, including bronchitis and pneumonia. However, it is less commonly associated with pneumonia compared to other pathogens."
    },
