    "id": "notion-microbiology-0091",
    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 91,
    "stem": "How is this case of subcutaneous mycosis treated?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Amphotericin B treatment"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Infection is self limiting"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Potassium iodide saturated solution"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Oral Itraconazole"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Oral itraconazole is considered the treatment of choice for sporotrichosis. It is an azole antifungal medication with good efficacy against Sporothrix schenckii. It is generally well-tolerated and is preferred over potassium iodide. Treatment duration may vary depending on the extent and severity of the infection.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Amphotericin B is an antifungal medication used for severe systemic fungal infections. However, for subcutaneous mycosis like sporotrichosis, it is not typically the first-line treatment. It may be considered for systemic cases or those not responding to other antifungal agents.",
      "B": "In some cases, the infection is self-limited. Although oral administration of saturated solution of potassium iodide in milk is quite effective, it is difficult for many patients to tolerate. The treatment of choice is oral itraconazole or another azole. For systemic disease, amphotericin B is given.",
      "C": "Oral administration of a saturated solution of potassium iodide (SSKI) has been used historically for sporotrichosis. However, its use is associated with side effects, and it may not be well-tolerated by all patients. It is considered an alternative treatment.",
      "D": "Oral itraconazole is considered the treatment of choice for sporotrichosis. It is an azole antifungal medication with good efficacy against Sporothrix schenckii. It is generally well-tolerated and is preferred over potassium iodide. Treatment duration may vary depending on the extent and severity of the infection."
    },
