    "id": "notion-microbiology-0098",
    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 98,
    "stem": "Situation 28- Eight hours after eating in a fiesta, Anna developed nausea and vomiting, headache, profuse diarrhea and low grade fever. Blood culture was negative for growth but the stool culture was positive. Repeated blood culture remained negative while stool culture was positive even 2 weeks after the initial examination. What was the MOST PROBABLE “growth” in the stool culture?",
