    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "SIMILAR TO PREVIOUS BOARD EXAM\nCONCEPT/PRINCIPLE. Neisseria are\ndiplococci, vibrios are comma shaped, and\ncampylobacteria are spiral shaped. Neisseria\nand vibrios are all oxidase positive. Because\ncampylobacter is grown\nunder unique conditions and temperature (42\nC), it is identified by just growing. It has both a\npoorly functioning oxidase and catalase.\nProteus and Escherichia are rod shaped and\nboth are oxidase negative. Escherichia is the\nonly one of the two that is a lactose fermenter.",
