    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Hemorrhagic necrosis of skin occurs often in\nsepsis caused by P aeruginosa; the lesions,\ncalled ecthyma gangrenosum, are surrounded\nby erythema and often do not contain pus.\nEcthyma is a deep form of impetigo and is\ncaused by S pyogenes or S aureus. Weil's\ndisease is the severe form of leptospirosis and\nRitter's disease is known as Stap scalded skin\nsyndrome.",
