    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Page 44 of Topnotch Handout. The fusion\nprotein of RSV causes the cells to fuse forming\nmultinucleated giant cells called syncytia\nhence giving rise to the name of the\nvirus.Surface spikes are fusion proteins not\nhemaglutinins and neuraminadases. It is an\nenveloped virus with a helical nucleocapsid It\nhas one piece of single-stranded, negative\npolarity RNA",
