    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 276,
    "stem": "A 72 year old female presents to your clinic with\ncomplaints of dyspnea, high grade fever and productive\ncough. Further history revealed associated symptoms of\nheadache, myalgia, abdominal pain, and diarrhea. Vital\nsigns: BP=140/90, HR=88, RR=28 T=40 degrees Celsius.\nWhich of the following significant findings would most\nlikely be in the patient’s history?",
