    "subject": "microbiology",
    "originalNumber": 289,
    "stem": "A 35 year old woman with a history of recurrent urinary\ntract infection comes to the ER due to dysuria\naccompanied by frequency and urgency. Urinalysis was\ndone which showed an alkaline urine, pyuria and the\npresence of numerous struvite crystals. The cause of her\nUTI is likely to be which of the following?",
