    "explanation": "This most likely a case of epiglottitis.\nSymptoms include fever, hoarseness, drooling\nwith a preference for tripod position. The\nincidence of epiglottitis due to H. influenzae\nhas been decreasing due to immunization.\nCharacteristic radiologic findings inclue the\nthumb sign. Endoscopy will show a cherry red\nepiglottis Treatment involves airway\nprotection and antibiotics (ceftriaxone,\nampicillin)",
