    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Staphylococcus aureus is catalase positive and\ncoagulase positive. The latter as well as the\nability to ferment mannitol makes S aureus\ndistinct from other staphylococcus species.\nTSST 1 is the superantigen toxin of S aureus.\nPVL on the otherhand, does not stimulate MHC\ntype II bearing cells but they form pores to\nWBC leading cytolysis. resistance to\nmethicillin is independent of beta lactamase\nprocuduction. it is secondary to chromosomal\nmediated decrease affinity PBP2a. Jawets 25th\ned p 186.",
