    "explanation": "Sulfatide is also an exported repetitive\nprotein. Cord factor on the other hand is the\nmost important virulence factor that\nprevents leukocyte migration. It is made up of\nglycolipid molecules that influence the long\nand slender formation of MTB bacilli.\nTuberculin surface protein is responsible for\neliciting the delayed hypersensitivity in TB.\nMurein simply refers to the peptidoglycan\nfound in bacterial cell walls.",
