    "stem": "A 57-year-old man with multiple myeloma comes to the\nphysician because of a 12-hour history of fever, sharp\nchest pain with deep inspiration, and cough productive\nof blood-tinged sputum. His temperature is 38.3 C (101\nF), blood pressure is 120/78 mm Hg, pulse is 112/min,\nand respirations are 28/min. Crackles are heard at the\nright lung base. His hemoglobin level is 9.2 g/dL,\nleukocyte count is 2600/mm3, and platelet count is\n6,000/mm3. Empiric antibiotics should be directed\nagainst which of the following organisms?",
