    "explanation": "The patient has acute filariasis. Presenting\nwith filarial fever, acute adenolymphangitis\nand nocturnal wheezing. This usually\nprogresses to a chronic disease, characterized\nby lymphedema, causing hydrocoele and/or\nelephantiasis. Thick blood smear is usally\ndone between 8PM and $am because the\nkinky or curved microfilariae exhibit\nnocturnal periodicity. This is endemic in\nSamar.",
