    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Answer: D. Vibrio vulnificus\nNotes: Vibrio vulnificus is responsible for\nsepticemia after consumption of contaminated\nraw oysters. Infections are most severe in\npatients with hepatic disease, hematopoietic\ndisease, or chronic renal failure and those\nreceiving immunosuppressive drugs.\nMortality in patients with septicemia can be as\nhigh as 50% unless antimicrobial therapy is\nstarted rapidly.",
