    "explanation": "Answer: B. Staphylococcus aureus\nNotes: Scalded Skin Syndrome is the\ndermatitis associated with the effects of the\nexfoliative toxin produced by strains of\nStaphylococcus aureus. The exfoliatin\nproduced acts in humans to disrupt the\nadhesive forces between cells of the stratum\ngranulosum, creating large flaccid bullae. This\nsyndrome occurs primarily in infants and\nchildren, with the primary infection usually\nunrelated to the areas where lesions appear.",
