    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Answer: B. Chlamydia psittaci\nNotes: Chlamydia psittaci is the etiologic agent\nof Psittacosis, an infection of birds and\nmammals that is transmissible to humans\ncausing pneumonia-like illness acquired\nthrough inhalation of infectious dropping\nfrom birds, parrots and parakeets. Laboratory\ndiagnosis involves detection of inclusion\nbodies called Levinthal-Cole-Lillie bodies\nstained with Giemsa or Macchiavello stain.\nThese inclusion bodies are more diffuse and\nirregular in shape containing little glycogen\nand do not stain recognizably with iodine as\ncompared to Halberstadter-Prowazek bodies\nof Chlamydia trachomatis.",
